# Implement Course Creation Feature

The "Create New Course" button in the instructor dashboard is currently a non-functional UI element. No course creation page exists in the frontend.

## Proposed Changes

### [Frontend] [Instructor Dashboard]

#### [NEW] [new/page.tsx](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-frontend/src/app/(dashboard)/instructor/courses/new/page.tsx)
- Create a new page with a form to add a course (Title, Description, Price, Status).
- Use `react-hook-form` for form management and `zod` for validation.
- Integrate with the `POST /api/courses` backend endpoint.
- Provide feedback to the user upon success or failure.

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-frontend/src/app/(dashboard)/instructor/courses/page.tsx)
- Wrap the "Create New Course" button with a `Link` component pointing to `/instructor/courses/new`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None planned for now, but will verify via manual browser testing.

### Manual Verification
1. Navigate to "Manage Courses" in the instructor dashboard.
2. Click "Create New Course".
3. Verify that the new course creation page is displayed.
4. Fill in the form and submit.
5. Verify that the course is successfully created and the user is redirected back to the course list.
6. Verify that the new course appears in the list.
